        "id": 6585
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-16T23:12:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you explain more about libaom\u0027s behavior? Why does it tend to underestimate? Because keyframe is at a smaller size, so a low QP is used to encode inter frames?\n\nOr if libaom does not underestimate, why could we see better coding performances?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 792,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 795,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "34eb963ec694e46d9122e2938791be3a4afe302a",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "837c259a_b49f83b6",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 795,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T02:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Because keyframe is at a smaller size, so a low QP is used to encode inter frames?\n\nCorrect, that is my understanding as well. From looking at encoded bitstreams, when the keyframe is encoded at a much lower quality than the inter-coded frame, inter-coded block candidates tend to be more expensive to code due to complex residuals (because the keyframe is overall more distorted than usual, so residuals have to compensate instead).\n\nThe end result is that I see is that for a given QP, libaom uses inter-encoded blocks more often than it should be, which causes the SSIMULACRA 2 efficiency curve to be worse.\n\nDoes this make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "77633194_de70d617",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 792,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 795,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "34eb963ec694e46d9122e2938791be3a4afe302a",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04f682be_2372c0cc",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 795,
      "author": {
        "id": 6585
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T23:14:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The encoder tends to pick inter modes than intra modes. That is true in many cases. So in general, I think adding a penalty to inter modes so that intra modes can be picked more often is reasonable.",
      "parentUuid": "837c259a_b49f83b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 792,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 795,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "34eb963ec694e46d9122e2938791be3a4afe302a",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
